{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-63874",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The number $16%$ (expressed as a decimal) is equal to $0.16.$ Therefore, a decrease of $16%$ corresponds to multiplication by a factor of:\n\n$$\n1-0.16=0.84\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ year, value of the home was $150\\,000\\cdot (0.84)$ dollars.\n\n- After $2$ years, value of the home was $150\\,000\\cdot (0.84)^{2}$ dollars.\n\n- After $3$ years, value of the home was  $150\\,000\\cdot (0.84)^{3}$ dollars.\n\n- After $4$ years, value of the home was $150\\,000\\cdot (0.84)^{4}$ dollars.\n\nEvaluating the last expression gives:\n\n$$\n150\\,000\\cdot (0.84)^{4}≈74\\,681\n$$\n\nSo, the home was worth $$74\\,681$ (to the nearest dollar) after $4$ years.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
